Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:05.00,Header,,0,0,0,,This is a Gentlemen of the Hàn free fansub.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.78,0:00:07.82,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,1500,5740,7020)\pos(653.755,355)}Episode 60
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.78,0:00:07.82,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,1500,5740,7020)\pos(653.755,524.455)}The Death of Cáo Cāo
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.02,0:00:32.40,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, masters Ma Liang and Yi Ji are here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.42,0:00:36.02,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(972.571,467.429)}Liú Bèi\NStyled: Xuándé
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.61,0:00:36.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Call them in.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.86,0:00:37.92,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.30,0:00:43.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Please rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.82,0:00:47.84,Default,,0,0,0,,How fare Jing Province and Yunchang?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.84,0:00:52.37,Default,,0,0,0,,General Guan fell for Lu Xun's trap and moved most of the Jing army to siege Fancheng.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.37,0:00:55.98,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Lü Meng crossed the river disguised as merchants \Nand captured the beacon towers,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.99,0:00:58.05,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,and then seized Jing Province!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.22,0:01:04.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Jing Province is lost!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.14,0:01:10.42,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,4840,5260)\pos(957.714,483.429)}Yī Jí\NStyled: Jìbó
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.21,0:01:09.29,Default,,0,0,0,,General Guan was hit by a poison arrow from Cao Ren and is wounded.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.29,0:01:12.56,Default,,0,0,0,,He is now reassembling troops to retake Jing Province.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.56,0:01:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,General Guan ordered us to return to Chengdu to seek aid.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.42,0:01:26.78,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,5940,6340)\pos(321.143,467.429)}Zhūgě Liàng\NStyled: Kǒngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.73,0:01:34.40,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.52,0:01:41.31,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord! Strategos!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.16,0:01:45.57,Default,,0,0,0,,General Liao, please rise. General Liao, please rise!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.24,0:01:49.23,Default,,0,0,0,,General Guan was trapped in Maicheng.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.23,0:01:51.27,Default,,0,0,0,,He ordered me to break out and seek help.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.78,0:01:56.58,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,6420,6780)\pos(955.2,473.6)}Liào Huà\NStyled: Yuánjiǎn
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.13,0:01:53.20,Default,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.00,0:02:00.96,Default,,0,0,0,,But Liu Feng and Meng Da did not send any reinforcements!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.96,0:02:06.49,Default,,0,0,0,,If such is the case, then Second Brother is doomed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.27,0:02:11.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Those two cannot atone for\N their insolence, even by death.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.63,0:02:15.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Please rest assured, my lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.49,0:02:18.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I shall lead troops to salvage Jing Province.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.97,0:02:25.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Should anything happen to Yunchang, then I cannot live with myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.77,0:02:37.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I will lead an army to rescue Yunchang myself tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.60,0:02:39.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Strategos, muster the troops
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.51,0:02:42.68,Default,,0,0,0,,and send a man to Langzhong to inform Yide.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.56,0:02:44.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.74,0:02:48.04,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.04,0:02:52.06,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,My lord! General Guan left Maicheng for Linju overnight, but was caught by Wu!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.06,0:02:56.34,Default,,0,0,0,,General Guan and his son chose\N to die rather than yield to Sun Quan!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.95,0:03:04.17,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.26,0:03:07.50,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,1860,2220)\pos(334,506)}Sūn Quán\NStyled: Zhòngmóu
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.98,0:03:08.08,Default,,0,0,0,,How so?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.61,0:03:13.76,Default,,0,0,0,,At present, Cao Cao, with\N a million strong host, covets Jiangnan.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.66,0:03:12.38,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,2300,2700)\pos(963.2,504)}Zhāng Zhāo\NStyled: Zǐbù
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.76,0:03:16.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Liu Bei, yearning for revenge for Guan Yu,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.43,0:03:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,will ally himself with Cao Cao to attack Jiangdong.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.53,0:03:27.60,Default,,0,0,0,,If these two men invade in unison, then Wu will be in grave danger.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.30,0:03:37.67,Default,,0,0,0,,We should hand over Guan Yu's head to Cao Cao,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.26,0:03:43.67,Default,,0,0,0,,thus deceiving Liu Bei into believing that \Nthe killing of Guan Yu was bidden by Cao Cao.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.14,0:03:46.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Liu Bei will certainly abhor Cao Cao,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.74,0:03:54.13,Default,,0,0,0,,and the troops of Shu will \Nbe directed to Wei, instead of our Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.08,0:04:13.39,Default,,0,0,0,,With this, my lord only needs to observe for the time being.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.39,0:04:15.97,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the best strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.30,0:04:27.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Good. I will send an emissary to send \NGuan Yu's head to Luoyang overnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.02,0:04:33.70,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,2300,2660)\pos(971.2,504)}Cáo Cāo\NStyled: Mèngdé
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.69,0:04:35.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Call in the emissary of Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.84,0:05:02.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Greetings, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.90,0:05:08.08,Default,,0,0,0,,The Marquis of Wu has sent me to gift Guan Yu's head to Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.02,0:05:30.38,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(318.4,489.6)}Sīmǎ Yí\NStyled: Zhòngdá
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.74,0:05:33.06,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(289.6,456)}Jiá Xǔ
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.65,0:05:52.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Lord Yunchang, how nice to see you again.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.48,0:06:00.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.55,0:06:03.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry, close the wooden box, hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.71,0:06:13.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, do not be alarmed! Your Highness, do not be alarmed!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.62,0:06:15.95,Default,,0,0,0,,General Guan is truly godlike!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.95,0:06:19.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, when the Marquis of Wu\N held a banquet a few days ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.93,0:06:25.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Lü Meng slandered Your Highness, and then suddenly died.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.09,0:06:32.37,Default,,0,0,0,,As I see it, General Guan's restless spirit possessed Lü Meng!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.61,0:06:37.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Guan Yu caused fear in life;
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.44,0:06:39.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}he causes fear in death;
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.65,0:06:42.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}and to revive after dying is most fearsome!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.20,0:06:43.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Hurry, hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.32,0:06:47.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Carve a body out of agarwood, and offer livestock and wine!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.54,0:06:50.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Give him a noble's burial outside Luoyang's south gate!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.50,0:06:53.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}All officials of any rank must attend the funeral!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.09,0:06:55.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}I, too, shall go there and worship him!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.46,0:06:56.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.73,0:07:02.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}General Guan!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.06,0:07:06.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}I hereby make you the Prince of Jing
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.02,0:07:10.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}and assign men to guard your tomb!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.32,0:07:22.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Yunchang, my second brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.90,0:07:22.94,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(640,149.333)}Spirit Tablet of Guan Yu, \NMarquis of Hanshou and Tiger General
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.08,0:07:38.89,Default,,0,0,0,,With you dying in regret, \Nhow can I enjoy glory by myself?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.67,0:07:37.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder Uncle!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.18,0:07:42.06,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(793.6,494.4)}Guān Xīng\NStyled: Ānguó
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.26,0:07:44.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Young Guan Xing!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.13,0:08:20.79,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, worry not.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.95,0:08:25.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}As ancient wisdom says,\N "death and life are destined."
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.20,0:08:28.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Yunchang was unyielding but proud,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.77,0:08:30.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}and thus such tragedy befell him.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.00,0:08:37.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}My lord, you should look after your health, in order to seek revenge later.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.22,0:08:43.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}When I swore at the Peach Garden with Yunchang and Yide,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.09,0:08:45.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}we swore to live and die together.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.35,0:08:47.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Now that Yunchang has passed,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.96,0:08:52.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}how can I enjoy glory by myself?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.73,0:08:59.17,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.17,0:09:03.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I shall not live under the same\N sun and moon as Eastern Wu!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.15,0:09:09.46,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,My lord, scouts have reported,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.46,0:09:13.30,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Eastern Wu offered Yunchang's head to Cao Cao.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.25,0:09:18.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Cao buried him with noble honors.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.12,0:09:21.14,Default,,0,0,0,,What is the meaning of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.76,0:09:26.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Cao saw through Eastern Wu's plan of shifting blame.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.92,0:09:31.77,Default,,0,0,0,,He buried Yunchang to \Nmake you foster hatred towards Eastern Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.43,0:09:41.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Pity my Yunchang, his head and body in two places!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.74,0:09:46.91,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(971.2,227.2)}General of\N the Five Tigers,\NMarquis of Hanshou,\NSpirit Tablet \Nof Guan Yu
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.52,0:09:58.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Muster the army against Eastern Wu and exact revenge!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.16,0:10:01.70,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, do not!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.41,0:10:07.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Right now, Wu wants us to invade Wei \Nwhilst Wei wants us to attack Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.16,0:10:09.87,Default,,0,0,0,,They both have their own interests.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.63,0:10:15.28,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, you should stay put \Nand hold a funeral for Yunchang.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.20,0:10:20.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Our best chance is to attack when Wu \Nand Wei are fighting against each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.48,0:10:36.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, I will go outside the \Nsouthern gate to hold a memorial ceremony.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.53,0:10:42.71,Default,,0,0,0,,All military personnel will wear \Nmourning clothes for Yunchang.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.28,0:10:49.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Second Brother, oh, Second Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.07,0:10:57.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Second Brother, oh, Second Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.90,0:11:03.14,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,3940,4220)\pos(323.2,476.8)}Zhāng Fēi\NStyled: Yìdé
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.16,0:11:05.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Second Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.89,0:11:13.84,Thinking,,0,0,0,,After Cao Cao buried Guan Yu,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.84,0:11:16.58,Thinking,,0,0,0,,his mind was restless each night.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.58,0:11:19.72,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,It was said that the old hall of the imperial abode in Luoyang
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.72,0:11:23.23,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,often made strange sounds as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.73,0:11:28.09,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Cao Cao decided to build a new hall to live in.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.09,0:11:29.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Good!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.34,0:11:35.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Su Yue, you do indeed have a sharp mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.20,0:11:37.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, you overpraise me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.91,0:11:43.41,Default,,0,0,0,,This sketch is satisfactory,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.65,0:11:48.66,Default,,0,0,0,,but there is nothing fit for the pillars and beams.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.34,0:11:51.58,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(320.4,478.4)}Sū Yuè
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.96,0:11:50.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.90,0:11:53.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Thirty{\i1} lǐ{\i0} from this city,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.86,0:11:57.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}there is a pool. It is named\N the Pool of the Leaping Dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.62,0:12:01.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}In the front of the pool, there is the Temple of the Leaping Dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.68,0:12:05.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Next to the temple, there is a pear tree
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.37,0:12:09.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}over ten {\i1}zhàng{\i0} tall. It can be used to build the beams of the palace.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.37,0:12:09.28,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,1 {\i1}zhàng{\i0}（丈）≈ 23.1 cm in Hàn Dynasty.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.14,0:12:16.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Good! Hurry and send men to the \NLeaping Dragon Pool to cut it down.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.42,0:12:17.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.17,0:12:42.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, I am guilty, I am guilty!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.14,0:12:44.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Why so frightened?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.10,0:12:48.56,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,That pear tree could not be hacked by iron saws nor steel axes!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.56,0:12:50.22,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,It cannot be cut down!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.06,0:12:55.20,Default,,0,0,0,,How can that be?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.66,0:13:00.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I will go see it myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.08,0:13:02.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Right there!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.16,0:13:20.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.28,0:13:42.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Good! A tree befitting a palace beam!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.13,0:13:45.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Good!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.03,0:14:00.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Chop it down.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.34,0:14:03.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, do not cut it!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.03,0:14:06.49,Default,,0,0,0,,This tree cannot be cut down, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.49,0:14:14.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Axes and saws cannot cut into this tree, \NYour Highness! This tree cannot be cut down!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.09,0:14:16.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.27,0:14:22.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, do not cut it! This tree cannot be cut down, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.98,0:14:23.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Silence!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.23,0:14:30.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I have traveled the realm for over forty years.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.09,0:14:35.18,Default,,0,0,0,,From the Emperor to the commoner, \Nthere are none who do not fear me!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.18,0:14:37.92,Default,,0,0,0,,What kind of demon or deity dares to disobey my will?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.37,0:14:57.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.34,0:15:15.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Does Your Highness know of \NHua Tuo, the legendary doctor?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.33,0:15:18.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.90,0:15:25.54,Default,,0,0,0,,The Hua Tuo who cured Zhou Tai of Jiangdong?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.54,0:15:26.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.81,0:15:33.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I have heard of his fame,\N but how is his medical expertise?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.78,0:15:38.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Hua Tuo, styled Yuanhua, is from Qiao Commandery of Pei.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.49,0:15:42.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}He is proficient in healing, a rarity in this world.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.75,0:15:46.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}There have been no patients that he was unable to treat.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.20,0:15:51.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}He also has the extraordinary ability to cut open a patient's stomach and cure the disease.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.53,0:15:55.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}He cuts stomachs open?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.86,0:15:57.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.06,0:15:59.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}If one suffered from an internal disease,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.39,0:16:04.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}then if medication was ineffective,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.13,0:16:06.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}he would have them ingest a numbing soup.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.28,0:16:08.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}They would then fall asleep like being drunk or dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.96,0:16:12.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}After that, he would use a knife to cut open the belly
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.48,0:16:15.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}and use medicine and herbs to wash the organs.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.02,0:16:17.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}The patient will feel no pain whatsoever.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.64,0:16:22.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}After washing it, he stitches it up
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.73,0:16:25.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}and applies medicine on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.27,0:16:28.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}In one month or twenty days,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.11,0:16:31.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}their health will revert back to normal.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.25,0:16:37.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}The world really has such a miracle healer?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.73,0:16:43.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Hua Tuo can be said to be Bian Que and the Granary Master reborn.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.73,0:16:43.41,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Bian Que and Chunyu Yi (the Granary Master) were prominent Chinese doctors famed for treating diseases.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.41,0:16:44.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is this man?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.93,0:16:49.20,Default,,0,0,0,,He lives in the capital, not far from here. \NYour Highness, why not summon him?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.69,0:16:52.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Summon Hua Tuo at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.54,0:16:53.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.85,0:17:20.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Your headache is due to strokes. \NThe root of the illness is in the skull.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.86,0:17:16.86,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,2620,2980)\pos(322,494)}Huà Tuó\NStyled: Yuánhuà
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.72,0:17:29.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, you understand the cause\N of the illness, you must be able to cure it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.37,0:17:38.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless the tumor in the brain is removed,\N medications will not work.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.21,0:17:47.27,Default,,0,0,0,,If this is the case, is my illness incurable?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.63,0:17:49.42,Default,,0,0,0,,No, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.62,0:17:54.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a method that can cure this illness once and for all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.05,0:18:08.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}First, drink the numbing soup.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.25,0:18:14.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Then, I will chop open the skull with a sharp axe
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.84,0:18:17.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}and take out the tumor...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.18,0:18:31.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Cut my skull open with a sharp axe? \NHow clever, how clever!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.64,0:18:36.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Yes, I would cut the skull open and take out the tumor.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.10,0:18:38.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}The source of the illness is thus removed.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.03,0:18:39.21,Default,,0,0,0,,The gall!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.54,0:18:43.88,Default,,0,0,0,,You... put down the axe! Put it down!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.76,0:18:52.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you intend to kill me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.04,0:18:54.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Calm down, Your Highness!\NCalm down, your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.36,0:18:55.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.27,0:19:03.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Has Your Highness heard that when Guan Yunchang was hit by a poison arrow in the right arm,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.74,0:19:05.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I scraped his bone to remove the poison for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.94,0:19:10.10,Default,,0,0,0,,He drank and played {\i1}weiqi{\i0} with \NMa Liang without a single bit of fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.10,0:19:14.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Your illness is minor, why be so fearful and suspicious?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.41,0:19:15.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Nonsense!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.45,0:19:21.62,Default,,0,0,0,,A painful arm can be scraped, \Nbut how can a skull be cut open?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.62,0:19:24.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness. Your Highness, calm down, calm down!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.21,0:19:38.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir Hua Tuo must've held friendly relations with Guan Yu.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.23,0:19:42.97,Default,,0,0,0,,So now you seek to avenge him! Correct?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.97,0:19:47.67,Default,,0,0,0,,No, Your Highness, it is a misunderstanding!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.35,0:19:49.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Men.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.58,0:19:55.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Jail this man for interrogation!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.02,0:19:56.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.34,0:19:57.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.06,0:20:01.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.63,0:20:06.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.34,0:20:09.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Such an excellent doctor is rare in the world!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.05,0:20:09.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.68,0:20:15.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You absolutely must not harm him!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.36,0:20:15.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.01,0:20:22.35,Default,,0,0,0,,That man intends to harm me. I will have no mercy!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.56,0:20:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.08,0:20:41.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you bringing food for Doctor Hua?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.38,0:20:45.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell Doctor Hua to eat it while it's hot.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.51,0:20:48.21,Default,,0,0,0,,How can he not eat anything after being beaten?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.21,0:20:49.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.44,0:21:00.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.21,0:21:14.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Doctor Hua, eat it while it's hot.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.72,0:21:16.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Doctor Hua!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.77,0:21:19.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Doctor Hua!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.19,0:21:26.96,Default,,0,0,0,,He has a high fever. Go get a piece of wet cloth.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.02,0:21:37.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, to remove the root of the illness,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.76,0:21:39.26,Default,,0,0,0,,the skull must be opened...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.43,0:21:44.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you still saying that? \NDo you want to die?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.31,0:21:52.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Die? One will die, if the illness isn't treated.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.01,0:21:54.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Treated...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.45,0:21:57.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Treated... treated...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.81,0:22:01.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Even beaten, you still haven't \Nforgotten about treating people.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.31,0:22:00.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Treated...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.54,0:22:02.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Treated...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.28,0:22:13.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Come, Doctor Hua, drink some hot water.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.65,0:22:53.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.14,0:23:00.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You suspect that I want to harm you. Me? Harm you?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.20,0:23:07.82,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I have not, I have not!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.82,0:23:11.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop rambling, you are out of your wits!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.23,0:23:26.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Suspicion is an illness too.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.76,0:23:30.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Treat it, treat it, treat it.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.45,0:24:04.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Wenhe, Ziyu,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.10,0:24:08.34,Default,,0,0,0,,this New Year's Eve is quite lively.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.79,0:24:15.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}The Nuo dance of exorcism is quite magnificent.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.79,0:24:17.97,Note (Potential style?),,0,0,0,,Note: Nuó dance or opera (儺戲) is an ancient Chinese folk opera still practiced today in the southern regions of China. Notable for its use of monstrous masks and ritualistic performance to exorcise evil.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.55,0:24:18.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}I hope Your Highness will get better
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.34,0:24:22.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}to destroy Wu and Shu and unite the land!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:53.40,0:24:58.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Once a year, the palace has the grand event\N of chasing away spirits through dance.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.71,0:25:01.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}We are seeing it right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.61,0:25:07.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}I hope the coming year will have \Ngood weather and abundant harvests!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:07.94,0:25:12.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Let it be such a year!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.56,0:25:33.70,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Your Highness, Eastern Wu has sent an envoy
Dialogue: 0,0:25:33.70,0:25:35.50,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,to deliver a letter from Sun Quan.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:46.14,0:25:51.44,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Your servant, Sun Quan, has long known that \Nthe Mandate of Heaven now favors the King of Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.44,0:25:53.70,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}I hope you shall ascend to the Great Throne,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:53.70,0:25:57.49,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}eradicate Liu Bei, and pacify the two Riverlands.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.49,0:26:02.69,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}Then, I will immediately submit to you with all my people and land.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:15.76,0:26:18.30,Default,,0,0,0,,That green-eyed lout!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:18.30,0:26:22.66,Default,,0,0,0,,He wants me to roast myself on top of a furnace fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.38,0:26:42.58,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,400,1820,2180)\pos(317.714,438.857}Chén Qún\NStyled: Chángwén
Dialogue: 0,0:26:41.18,0:26:42.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.76,0:26:44.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}The Han Empire has been in terminal decline.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:44.93,0:26:48.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14)}But you hold monumental virtues and the hopes of all the masses.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:48.57,0:26:51.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Today, Sun Quan has bowed down in submission.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:51.10,0:26:55.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}This is proof of the will of Heaven \Nand the people, who clamor in unison.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.92,0:26:58.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Your Highness must heed Heaven and the people!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:58.56,0:27:00.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Ascend the Great Throne now!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:00.73,0:27:04.84,Default,,0,0,0,,May Your Highness ascend to the Great Throne!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:09.54,0:27:14.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}I have served the House of Han for many years.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:14.50,0:27:17.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Although I have virtuous deeds and the people's will,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.30,0:27:21.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}I am already the King of Wei.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.46,0:27:27.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}With my fame at its zenith, \Nhow can I have higher aspirations?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.78,0:27:35.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Supposing the Mandate of Heaven is with me,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:35.20,0:27:41.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}then let me be King Wen of Zhou.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:41.50,0:27:44.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness is most wise!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:48.20,0:27:52.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, now that Sun Quan has submitted,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.55,0:27:58.16,Default,,0,0,0,,you may grant him a position and a title. \NOrder him against Liu Bei.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:00.08,0:28:01.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:01.94,0:28:07.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I hereby appoint Sun Quan as "General of Fast Cavalry,"
Dialogue: 0,0:28:07.65,0:28:11.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Marquis of Nanchang, and Lord of Jing Province.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.64,0:28:14.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow, send an envoy to Eastern Wu.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:14.96,0:28:29.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Long live the King!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:40.76,0:28:44.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Doctor Hua, it's New Year's Day. Have some wine!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:45.65,0:28:46.82,Default,,0,0,0,,New Years?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:48.53,0:28:51.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Happy New Year, Bailiff Wu!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:51.22,0:28:53.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, thank you!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:53.75,0:29:00.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope that the year will be of good luck and prosperity, with all hopes being fulfilled.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:00.14,0:29:04.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Bailiff Wu! I will drink, I will drink.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.11,0:29:30.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Many thanks to you and your wife for bringing me meals every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:31.20,0:29:35.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Doctor, you are a miracle healer.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:35.50,0:29:40.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You cured people of diseases and saved many lives!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:46.58,0:29:48.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Miracle healer?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:50.51,0:29:55.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I have cured illnesses and saved people all my life,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:55.30,0:30:00.45,Default,,0,0,0,,but in the end, I cannot save myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:02.61,0:30:09.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I am lucky to have you care for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:11.79,0:30:15.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Drink some wine. Have another cup.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:22.77,0:30:26.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I know that I am about to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:31.81,0:30:40.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I regret that my {\i1}Book of the Blue Pocket{\i0} \Nhas not been passed onto the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:48.58,0:30:54.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I enjoy your kindness very much, yet I have nothing to repay you.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:02.54,0:31:06.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I have written a letter for my family.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:07.48,0:31:12.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Find someone to go to my home and get the {\i1}Book of the Blue Pocket.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:12.24,0:31:18.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I bequeath it to you so that you \Nmay pass on my skills of medicine.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.45,0:31:24.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, if I get this book, I will make sure to quit this job,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.18,0:31:29.73,Default,,0,0,0,,and focus on the art of medicine to pass on your virtue.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:10.32,0:32:15.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:15.30,0:32:20.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I have roamed the world for over thirty years, never believing in superstition.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:20.04,0:32:22.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Why has this happened today?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:24.89,0:32:30.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, Hua Tuo still lives! Why not give him a chance?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:30.29,0:32:34.63,Default,,0,0,0,,He wants to hurt me! He wants to open my skull and take my life!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:34.63,0:32:39.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Pass on my order! Interrogate Hua Tuo!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:39.09,0:32:44.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\}Your Highness, why not invite a Daoist priest to set up an altar and make prayers?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:46.18,0:32:49.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}As the Sage said,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:49.60,0:32:57.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}"Whoever offends Heaven cannot be prayed for."
Dialogue: 0,0:32:57.81,0:33:05.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}My destiny has run its course. How can I be saved?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:18.29,0:33:20.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't burn it! Don't burn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:20.56,0:33:22.43,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Why did you burn the {\i1}Book of the Blue Pocket?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:22.43,0:33:25.03,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,It is Doctor Hua's life work!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:25.03,0:33:30.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Even with all of his knowledge and wisdom,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.24,0:33:33.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Hua Tuo ended up dying in a prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:33.51,0:33:35.58,Default,,0,0,0,,What good is it to keep it?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:43.90,0:33:45.82,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(645.455,87.273)}The Tomb of\NDoctor Hua Tuo
Dialogue: 0,0:33:52.53,0:33:53.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Mister Hua!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:04.85,0:34:06.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:16.06,0:34:19.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I... I...
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.65,0:34:28.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness, you must nourish your health, so you may recover.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:35.83,0:34:45.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}I have traversed the realm for over thirty years,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:45.83,0:34:48.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}eliminating all rebel warlords.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:49.99,0:34:55.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Only Sun Quan of Jiangdong
Dialogue: 0,0:34:55.10,0:35:01.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}and Liu Bei of Western Shu remain.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:04.04,0:35:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}I am now ill,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:09.74,0:35:17.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}and I am unable to attend \Nto these matters with you gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:17.16,0:35:25.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}I entrust... I entrust you with my household matters.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:25.22,0:35:27.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:30.56,0:35:38.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Cao Ang, my eldest son, was born to Lady Liu.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:38.40,0:35:43.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}It is a pity he died at Wancheng.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:43.94,0:35:48.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Lady Bian has given birth to four sons:
Dialogue: 0,0:35:48.16,0:35:54.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Cao Pi, Cao Zhang, Cao Zhi, and Cao Xiong.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:54.00,0:35:59.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}I have adored my third son Cao Zhi for my whole life,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:01.24,0:36:04.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,670)}but he is superficial in nature,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:04.68,0:36:13.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}decadent, and inebriates himself often. \NHe cannot be made heir.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:13.93,0:36:19.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}My second son, Cao Zhang, is brave but witless.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:19.97,0:36:25.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}My fourth son, Cao Xiong, \Nis sickly and hard to nurse.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:34.46,0:36:38.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Only my eldest son, Cao Pi,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:38.29,0:36:44.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}is sincere, magnanimous, respectful, and cautious. He shall succeed me.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:44.09,0:36:50.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Gentlemen, you will support him.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:51.01,0:36:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:00.80,0:37:03.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}After I die,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.80,0:37:13.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}build seventy-two false tombs outside Jiangwu City in Zhangde.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:13.85,0:37:17.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}Do not let posterity know where I am buried.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:18.35,0:37:25.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not let posterity know where I am buried...
Dialogue: 0,0:37:26.06,0:37:27.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:38.93,0:37:41.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:38:01.04,0:38:06.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:15.57,0:38:17.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:39.08,0:38:40.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:48.88,0:38:50.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:59.10,0:39:00.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:08.42,0:39:12.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:20.01,0:39:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:31.06,0:39:32.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:32.19,0:39:38.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}After I die,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:38.53,0:39:46.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}you all shall learn needlework
Dialogue: 0,0:39:46.00,0:39:54.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}to make many silk shoes and\N sell them to sustain yourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:54.50,0:39:58.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}You all shall reside in \Nthe Bronze Sparrow Terrace
Dialogue: 0,0:39:58.59,0:40:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,660)}and make offerings every day,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:00.76,0:40:07.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord14}make sure to have performers play music and offer food.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:13.89,0:40:19.76,Thinking,,0,0,0,,In the 25th year of the Jian'an era, 220 CE,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:19.76,0:40:26.09,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Cao Cao passed away from his illness \Nat Luoyang, at sixty-six years of age.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:51.33,0:40:57.61,Thinking,,0,0,0,,{\bord14\pos(640,678.667)}Dim grows the flashing of swords and daggers,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:51.33,0:40:56.93,Song,,0,0,0,,{\k52}Àn{\k44}dàn{\k60}liao {\k77}dāo{\k64}guāng{\k146}jiàn{\k117}yǐng
